  "slug": "empece",
  "titulo": "-zar verbs in the preterite",
  "subtitulo": "Empecé a las seis; la clase empezó tarde.",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "In the preterite, -ar verbs ending in -zar change z to c in the yo form only (empecé, almorcé, crucé), because Spanish writes ce, not ze. All other forms keep the z: empezaste, empezó.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": null,
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Verbs ending in **-zar** are regular -ar verbs in the preterite, with **one spelling change**: in **yo**, the **z** becomes **c**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Why? Spanish almost never writes **ze**. Before **e** it writes **ce**, which sounds the same: **empecé**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "tabla",
          "encabezados": [
            "Person",
            "empezar",
            "almorzar",
            "cruzar"
          ],
          "filas": [
            [
              "yo",
              "empecé",
              "almorcé",
              "crucé"
            ],
            [
              "tú",
              "empezaste",
              "almorzaste",
              "cruzaste"
            ],
            [
              "él / ella / usted",
              "empezó",
              "almorzó",
              "cruzó"
            ],
            [
              "nosotros / nosotras",
              "empezamos",
              "almorzamos",
              "cruzamos"
            ],
            [
              "ellos / ellas / ustedes",
              "empezaron",
              "almorzaron",
              "cruzaron"
            ]
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Common ones: **empezar**, **comenzar**, **almorzar**, **cruzar**, **organizar**, **lanzar**, **abrazar**, **alcanzar**, **realizar**, **utilizar**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Empezar** and **almorzar** change their stem in the present (**empiezo**, **almuerzo**), but **not** in the preterite: **empecé**, **almorcé**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **z** and **e** don't get along in Spanish spelling, so **c** steps in whenever an **e** shows up."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
